& [Fault]
  + the independent evidence bundle passed under PowerShell 7 but Windows PowerShell 5.1 terminated while Git warned that one generated `.tmp` directory in the live Eclipse checkout was not readable
  + Git's inventory command remained semantically successful, but Windows PowerShell converted native stderr into a terminating error under the script's stop preference

& [Correction]
  + centralize Git inventory invocation in both custody scripts
  + capture stdout separately, suppress warning text from semantic inventory, restore the caller error preference, and continue to require an exact zero Git exit code
  + replay custody and the full evidence verifier under both PowerShell hosts

& [Boundary]
  + no inaccessible generated file is selected into semantic custody
  + warning suppression does not suppress nonzero Git exits or change the selected path count and digest
